# OS
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# IDE
.idea
.vscode

# Dependencies
node_modules

# Build
dist
build
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# Tooling caches
.nx

# Vendored dependency sources (opensrc skill) — for study only. Anchored: unanchored, it also matched
# .claude/skills/opensrc/ and lint-staged refused to re-stage the skill (2026-10-21).
/opensrc/

# Project material. Plans and spikes are the portfolio and DO ship; the rest must not.
#   resources/  — 170 MB, proprietary Euratlas vectors
#   spikes/*/out/ — the 21 GPL-3.0 world_*.geojson and other generated payloads
#   session-log.jsonl — this machine's activity log
#   claude-archive/ — dead design-system skills
files/*
!files/plans/
!files/spikes/
files/spikes/*/out/

# Historical borders — GPL-3.0 source, spike only (see files/spikes/fetch-borders).
# NOT `public/borders/`: a gitignore pattern containing a slash is anchored to the repository root,
# so that form silently stopped matching the day `public/` moved into `packages/atlas/`. The 21 GPL
# payloads were committed as a result. `**/` matches at any depth and survives the next move.
**/public/borders/

# Years saved by the Cartographer in local mode — the dev's working copies, never committed (his call,
# 2026-10-12: "ils sont pour nous pour travailler"). A year folder is ignored; `years/index.json` stays
# tracked, committed with `"years": []`, and is marked skip-worktree on the dev's machine so a local save
# listing a year does not show as a change (see known-issues.md). `*.tmp` covers a save cut off half-way.
**/public/years/*/
# Published by the dev's call, 2026-10-16: 1100 goes online as it stands, to show to a few people.
!**/public/years/1100/
**/public/years/*.tmp

# Turbo task cache
.turbo

# NPM
.npmrc

# Secrets (API keys, tokens)
**/.env*

# The Cartographer's autosave: drafts and hourly snapshots, local to the machine (CARTO-238)
**/.autosave/

# The contribution tool (Payload): Next's build folder, and its SQLite database — the dev's local working base,
# never committed. What ships is the export the atlas reads.
**/.next/
**/next-env.d.ts
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
